 "summary": "On 849 moments from 8 days of held-out walks in Hervanta, the top route held where the person really was 42% of the time after 5 minutes and 25% after 10 minutes; one of the shown routes did 44% of the time after 10 minutes (guessing at every fork: 11% and 18%). 98% of the moments started on a mapped path.",
 "note": "\"Right\" means within 20 m of the route line. Marker: distance from the closest route's \"probably here by now\" marker. With a ±15 m Bluetooth-mesh history the model's top route was right 35% / 21% of the time after 5 / 10 min. 90% intervals from resampling days, top route after 10 min: 19%–33%. Only 17 walks were long enough, so treat the numbers as rough.",
 "forkText": "A probability for each branch, from how sharp the turn is, whether the same path continues, path type, dead ends, marked hiking routes and how many other people walked each branch. On 619 real forks in Hervanta it put the most weight on the branch people really took 70% of the time (guessing: 32%, straightest: 67%)."
